@prompt
Hazel also has classic print-statement debugging. `print(value)` shows a value in the sidebar panel, then carries on. Sequence it with `;`.

# Task
The garden waters for a week. Add `print(daily);` inside `weekly_water` to log each daily amount, then watch the print panel fill as the calls below run.

@hint
`print(daily);` before the result, inside the function.

@reference
### Print
```hazel
print(42);
"done"
```
`print` writes a value to the sidebar panel and continues. Each entry shows a sequence number and a source line.

@code
let weekly_water(daily: Int): Int =
  daily * 7
in
weekly_water(250);
weekly_water(180);
weekly_water(50)
